CORE
main.c
--full-slice
^\[main.assertion.1\] line \d+ before the assumption: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.2\] line \d+ only reachable with i != 2: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
The full slicer must not remove an ASSUME false: it has no successors in the
control-flow graph, so that no instruction is control dependent on it, but
removing it makes the second assertion reachable with i == 2.
